@bank all
// SW6 (ending writer A), the crossing back (plans/ending-spec.html, E-1 and section 9; EN2 builds it). Sunday Day 35,
// 14:30, four weeks to the hour after the first crossing. Keys mirror event.crossingLine.* (content/banks/
// event-crossingLine.lines). Mail is "Subject | body", unsigned unless it says who. The staged scenes are meetings in
// content/ending/: crossingBackWord (Vance, Wed), crossingBackOath (you lead it), crossingBackSignal (Saruth),
// crossingBackAddress.stay | .go | .ask (the Captain's final address). CANON: the Wren crosses back over the Line;
// never "permission" or "leave" about the reach; every Veyli is they/them; the comet's Veyli name is never said.
// FLAGS read here (agreed with lead 39 / EN1): end.stay, end.go (settled at the address); end.now.stay | end.now.go |
// end.now.unsure (your answer so far, before the address).

// ---- Wednesday Day 31: Vance's word (said in person first: meeting crossingBackWord), then these as the record
// EN2 (RV21's should): the notice as Vance sets off to find you on Wednesday, and Sunday's fetch to the oath if
// you're not in the bow lounge by 14:35 (his notice, then his line beside you, a bubble: 60 at most)
== event.crossingBack.notice.vanceComing
- Commander Vance is coming to find you.
== event.crossingBack.notice.fetch
- Commander Vance is coming to find you: the oath is waiting for you.
== event.crossingBack.say.fetch
- There you are. The bow lounge. They won't start without you.
== event.crossingBack.notice.word
- Sunday at 14:30 the Wren crosses back over the Line. You're leading the oath.
== event.crossingBack.status.word
- Sunday: the Wren crosses back over the Line
== event.crossingBack.mail.word
- Sunday we cross back over the Line | On Sunday at 14:30 the Wren crosses back over the Line, four weeks to the hour after the first crossing. The ceremony is in the bow lounge. One first-timer: Cadet Bramwell. You will lead the oath, as discussed. Then the Line supper in the mess at 18:00. Attendance is not required. It is, however, expected. Vance
== event.crossingBack.tracked.word
- Sunday 14:30: lead the oath, the bow lounge

// ---- Wednesday to Saturday: the ship talks (bubbles, 60 at most; the mess and the Works bay; no arrow).
// EN2: say these while event:crossingBack is announced and before Sunday's horn. Crew remember Day 7.
== event.crossingBack.chatter
- Back over the Line on Sunday. Where did four weeks go?
- Four weeks in the reach. It went by like a Tuesday.   #funny
- Same punch both ways, I hear. Brennan won't say.   #funny
- I'll miss the names out here. Every star's got a story.   #warm
- Sunday's crossing back. I'm wearing the gold ribbon again.
- Remember the first crossing? Somebody cried. It was me.   #funny
- The new hand's leading the oath. A month ago they took it.   #warm
- Bad luck to cross on a full stomach? Asking for Pell.   #funny
- The charts get thick again on Sunday. Survey's in mourning.   #funny
- I've got used to the reach. Strange, going back.
? place:worksbay
- Coil three's heard we're crossing back. She's sulking.   #funny
- Calder's checking the ramp seals. For Sunday. For no reason.   #funny
? place:mess
- Brennan's ordering punch fruit. Or whatever's in it.   #funny
- Line supper again on Sunday. I'm saving myself.   #funny
? who:pell
- My fourth Line. Two in, two out. I'm practically a fish.   #funny
- Last time Tomas got the dregs. This time he drinks fresh.   #warm
? who:tomas
- I'm crossing this one. Properly. I've swapped my watch.   #warm
- Four weeks ago I was at the Deck 2 lift. Not this time.
? who:bramwell-basil
- What's the oath like? Is it long? Do I have to learn it?
- Is the punch really green? Pell says it's green. Is it?
- I'm the only first-timer. Is that good? It feels big.
? who:brennan
- Punch is made, love. Don't ask me what's in it.   #funny
? who:raman
- Tavessa's behind us now. Say goodbye to it from the stern.   #warm
? who:holt
- Back over the Line. I'll admit it. It was a good month.
? who:saruth
- The reach will be quieter when the Wren has crossed back.   #warm
? who:vance
- Ribbons by 14:00 on Sunday. Gold, both sides. Regulation.   #funny
? who:calder
- Sunday's a working day until half two. Then it isn't.
? tier>=friend
- You're leading it? Course you are. You'll be good.   #warm
- Nervous about Sunday? Don't be. Just read slowly.
- Don't rush the last line. It's the best one.   #warm

// ---- Saturday Day 34, 10:00: Taavek's ship comes back (notice, a level 2 arrow to the bow glass, once)
// EN2: the level 2 arrow's label to the glass (a place, as every arrow's)
== event.crossingBack.arrow.vessel
- Taavek's ship: the bow lounge, Deck 3
== event.crossingBack.notice.vessel
- Taavek's ship is off the bow again: the bow lounge glass, Deck 3.
== event.crossingBack.status.vessel
- Taavek's ship is flying with the Wren to the Line.
// Saruth at the glass (a bubble each as you arrive, in order; 60 at most), then the crew's at-the-glass lines
== event.crossingBack.glass.saruth.1
- Ah. You came to see them. So did I.
== event.crossingBack.glass.saruth.2
- They will fly with the Wren as far as the Line.
== event.crossingBack.glass.saruth.3
- Company, the other way. It is only courteous.   #warm
== event.crossingBack.glass.here
- That's the little ship? Running sweetly now, look.   #warm
- Our part's in there. Spinning. I like that.   #warm
- They came all the way back to walk us to the door.

// ---- Sunday Day 35: the crossing back
== event.crossingBack.notice.morning
- Today at 14:30 the Wren crosses back over the Line. You lead the oath, the bow lounge.
== event.crossingBack.notice.ceremony
- The crossing back: the oath in the bow lounge at 14:30. You're at the front this time.
== event.crossingBack.notice.horn
- The ship's horn: the Wren has crossed back over the Line.
== event.crossingBack.status.morning
- Today 14:30: the Wren crosses back over the Line.
== event.crossingBack.status.onset
- Crossed back over the Line. Supper 18:00.
== event.crossingBack.status.resolution
- Crossed back over the Line. Line supper, the mess, 18:00.
// the ring on the front of the bow lounge (EN2: "Lead the oath")
== event.crossingBack.ring.oath
- Lead the oath
// the banner at 14:30, after the horn (the Captain on every deck, briefly, as on Day 7)
== event.crossingBack.address.onset.1
- This is the Captain. We've crossed back over the Line.
== event.crossingBack.address.onset.2
- Thank the reach for a good month. Look out of a window while it's still there.
== event.crossingBack.address.onset.3
- Everyone who can, to the bow lounge. I've something to say after the oath. Marrow out.
// tap lines at the ceremony (crew), and the ask (crew asking you along, 14:00-14:30)
== event.crossingBack.gather.ceremony.here
- Front's yours today. We'll be at the back, laughing.   #funny
- Read it slowly. The Captain always does.
- Look at Basil. That was you, four weeks ago.   #warm
== event.crossingBack.gather.ceremony.ask
- Bow lounge at half two. You're at the front. Don't be late.
- You're leading it? Then I'm coming. Wouldn't miss it.   #warm
- Crossing back at half two. Gold ribbons. Bring Basil.
== event.crossingBack.gather.ceremony.thanks
- You stand at the front of the bow lounge and say the old oath, the stars at your back. Basil answers for the first-timers. Then a mug of Line punch, all of it, both ways now.   #warm
== event.crossingBack.tap.punch
- Brennan's Line punch. Green, faintly fizzy, as before. You know what's in it now.   #funny
// the plaque's second line (under Day 7's): Basil's answer (flag:back.answer.feel | .colonies | .slow in the meeting)
== event.crossingBack.plaque.feel
- The CSV Wren crossed back over the Line, Day 35. "We were new. We're not, quite. Thank you for having us."
== event.crossingBack.plaque.colonies
- The CSV Wren crossed back over the Line, Day 35. "The Ostrander colonies did it first. Not as well."
== event.crossingBack.plaque.slow
- The CSV Wren crossed back over the Line, Day 35. "Hello, reach. Thank you. Goodbye, reach."
== event.crossingBack.plaque.missed
- The CSV Wren crossed back over the Line, Day 35. "We came a long way, and we're going home the long way."
// the certificate's second date (the keepsake's tap text once both are on it), and the Record line
== event.crossingBack.keepsake
- Your Line certificate, signed by the Captain twice: "Crossed into the Veyli reach, Day 7. Crossed back, Day 35. This reach knows your name."
== event.crossingBack.record
- Crossed back over the Line, Day 35, and led the oath.
== event.crossingBack.record.missed
- Crossed back over the Line, Day 35.

// ---- the Line supper, 18:00-19:15, the mess (as on Day 7), coloured by your choice: flag:end.stay or flag:end.go
// (settled at the address). The Mail goes out at 16:00, after the address.
== event.crossingBack.gather.lineSupper.name
- The Line supper
== event.crossingBack.gather.lineSupper.mail
- The Line supper | The Line supper tonight at six, in the mess, the second this tour. Whatever the crew voted for, a pudding, and toasts. No punch. I promise again.
== event.crossingBack.gather.lineSupper.ask
- Line supper at six. Second one this tour. Same benches.
? flag:end.go
- Line supper at six. Sit with us. It's your last one.   #warm
? flag:end.stay
- Line supper at six. You're staying, so you're buying.   #funny
== event.crossingBack.gather.lineSupper.thanks
? flag:end.go
- The mess is full, every bench taken, and somehow there's room next to you all night. People keep raising cups your way.   #warm
? flag:end.stay
- The mess is full and loud. Every few minutes someone leans over to say they're glad you're staying.   #warm
?
- The mess is full again, every bench taken. Someone budges up, and someone else passes you a plate.   #warm
// the toasts (tap lines at the supper; card lines, 90 at most)
== event.crossingBack.gather.lineSupper.here
- To the reach, and to everyone who crossed it twice.   #warm
- Supper's to get rid of the taste again. Still works.   #funny
? flag:end.stay
- To {me}, who's staying. Selfishly, cheers.   #warm
- To the Wren, and the people who won't leave her.   #warm
- You're staying! Good. I'd run out of people to sit with.   #funny
- To the next four weeks, and the four after that.   #warm
- Staying! I owe Pell a biscuit. I bet you'd go.   #funny
? flag:end.go
- To {me}. Go and be brilliant. Then write.   #warm
- To headquarters, who don't know what they're getting.   #funny
- Last Line supper with you. I'm eating slowly.   #warm
- Here's to you. The Wren won't be the same. Better, a bit.   #funny
- To the one who led the oath, and leaves on the Tern.   #warm
== event.crossingBack.gather.lineSupper.chatter
- Second Line supper this tour. Seconds ran out in eight minutes.   #funny
? flag:end.stay
- The new hand's staying. You could hear the cheer on Deck 6.   #warm
? flag:end.go
- The new hand goes Monday. Nobody's said it at the table yet.   #warm
